To enjoy this game, buy it on a sale and don't expect good gameplay. This game was made to look pretty and be historic gore eye candy. The plot and historic accuracy is hilariously bad (the latter especially;
). This game is less historically than the '300' films but it is still epic.
Gameplay is relatively easy. Half is quick-time events where you will still kill the enemy even if you click the wrong button. You just won't get full XP for it.
The best feature of the game is its charming visuals and excessive spilling of blood. Story is short and simple with a lot of violent vendettas and Roman "death or glory" moments.
Overall, despite having lovely graphics, this game is still not worth its full price and will only be enjoyable on its first playthrough. We don't get many (if any) Roman hack and slash games which is why this made a nice change for me. But if I had the option, I won't neither rate this game up or down as the draw to this game is more or less purely cosmetic. Don't buy this game with high expectations of the gameplay. Just leave all logic and intelligence on the desk and enjoy this dumb bloodbath QTE game...

